ifferential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\n- **I.** $y' + \\frac{3 \\cdot y^{3}}{x^{2}} = 5 \\cdot \\sin{\\left(y \\right)}$\n- **II.** $y' - y \\cdot e^{x} = 5 \\cdot x^{2} \\cdot y^{5}$\n- **III.** $y' + 2 \\cdot y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/add "e6954ca4-0576-566d-ba72-0d26e66452ab" :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation I is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\n- Equation II is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=- e^{x},\\quad q(x)=5 \\cdot x^{2},\\quad n=5.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=2 \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)},\\quad q(x)=- 2 \\cdot x,\\quad n=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, select II, III."] [:db/add "e6954ca4-0576-566d-ba72-0d26e66452ab" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "e6954ca4-0576-566d-ba72-0d26e66452ab" :question/answer-fields "902c375f-f748-5a4d-a548-dbdefc54c9c1"] [:db/add "e6954ca4-0576-566d-ba72-0d26e66452ab" :question/answer-fields "5bea2f66-1e31-5fef-88db-6a6425f152d8"] [:db/add "e6954ca4-0576-566d-ba72-0d26e66452ab" :question/answer-fields "f28f64b6-0945-576e-993a-ff64ebcb50a6"] [:db/add "e6954ca4-0576-566d-ba72-0d26e66452ab" :question/answer-fields "89113077-dd44-5d5c-93df-87bb21b128c3"] [:db/ensure "e6954ca4-0576-566d-ba72-0d26e66452ab" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186147456 :knowledge-point/questions "e6954ca4-0576-566d-ba72-0d26e66452ab"] [:db/add "357812d6-6781-50d9-94b0-a785a18b1d32" :answer/id #uuid "357812d6-6781-50d9-94b0-a785a18b1d32"] [:db/add "357812d6-6781-50d9-94b0-a785a18b1